<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Huiwen of Qin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">356–311 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Huiwen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> from 338 to 311 BCE. He had the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shang-yang">Shang Yang</a> executed on his accession but kept his laws, and in 325 BCE became the first Qin ruler to take the title of king. With the diplomat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-yi">Zhang Yi</a> he played the eastern states against each other, and his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-cuo">Sima Cuo</a> conquered Ba and Shu in 316 BCE.</p></div>
